# model-server — copy to .env

# Which slots run (slot names, not model names).
COMPOSE_PROFILES=tts

# Folder name under stt/, tts/, or llm/ for each slot.
STT_MODEL=
TTS_MODEL=orpheus
LLM_MODEL=

# GPU index(es). On ace-h200 use 1 (GPU 0 is production).
GPU_DEVICE_IDS=0

# A gRPC front door for the STT slot, for callers that cannot hold a WebSocket
# (NVIDIA Cloud Functions has no WebSocket invocation path). UNSET IS OFF, and
# off is total: compose-files.sh does not name compose.grpc.yml, so the
# resolved config is identical to one from before the facade existed.
#
# It was missing from this file entirely, so a fresh checkout had no way to
# know the option existed and start-model-server.sh now asks instead.
USE_STT_GRPC=

# Only published port; model containers bind nothing on the host.
GATEWAY_PORT=8100

# Upstreams default to Compose service names. Uncomment to override.
# STT_UPSTREAM=http://stt:8001
# TTS_UPSTREAM=http://tts:8002
# LLM_UPSTREAM=http://llm:8003

# Weights (paths inside the container).
INDIC_NEMO_PATH=/app/models/IndicConformer.nemo
BHILI_ENABLE=no
BHILI_NEMO_PATH=

# HuggingFace cache / token (gated Parler tokenizer).
HF_CACHE_VOLUME=voicera-prod_hf_cache
HF_TOKEN=

# A token for one slot only, used in place of HF_TOKEN for that slot and
# nothing else. Leave them empty and every slot uses HF_TOKEN, which is what
# one account's token already covers.
#
# They exist for the two cases a single token cannot express: access to the
# gated repos granted to different HuggingFace accounts, and fine-grained
# tokens scoped to one repository each. start-model-server.sh offers the
# choice and writes whichever you pick here.
#
# The fallback is Compose's, not the script's -- each service resolves
# ${<SLOT>_HF_TOKEN:-${HF_TOKEN:-}} -- so an .env written before these existed
# behaves exactly as it did, and a stack driven by hand needs no new keys.
# The TTS value also reaches indic-mio's vLLM sidecar, which fills that slot.
STT_HF_TOKEN=
TTS_HF_TOKEN=
LLM_HF_TOKEN=

# vLLM limits for the LLM slot.
VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192
VLLM_MAX_NUM_SEQS=20
# Keep low on shared MPS GPUs (default 0.9 would starve other workers).
VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.10
# Empty means bf16.
VLLM_QUANTIZATION=

# Local AI4Bharat NeMo fork (build context). Only stt/indic-conformer's
# Dockerfile uses it -- `COPY --from=nemo` -- but Compose stats every declared
# build context whether or not a Dockerfile references it, so this must name a
# directory that EXISTS even when the selected model has no use for it.
#
# start-model-server.sh handles that: it clones the fork for indic-conformer,
# and points this at an empty placeholder for everything else. Set it by hand
# only when driving Compose without the script.
#
# This shipped as /home/kowshik/ai4bharat_nemo -- one person's home directory,
# so every fresh checkout inherited a path that existed on exactly one machine
# and failed the build with "failed to get build context nemo".
#
# git clone --branch nemo-v2 --depth 1 https://github.com/AI4Bharat/NeMo.git ~/ai4bharat_nemo
NEMO_CONTEXT_PATH=

# Two lines used to sit here, uncommented, from an old native-mode run: a
# RUN_MODE set to dev, and
#
#   TTS_UPSTREAM=http://127.0.0.1:8002
#
# Inside the gateway container 127.0.0.1 is the gateway, so that upstream sent
# every TTS request to a port nothing was listening on and /health reported
# "All connection attempts failed" for a tts container that was up and serving.
# The correct forms are commented out near the top of this file: the gateway
# reaches the slots by Compose service name, and leaving the variables unset is
# what selects that. RUN_MODE was read by nothing at all.
